<section class="page-section">
  <div class="shell split">
    <aside class="split__aside">
      <span class="eyebrow">II / Method</span>
      <h2>Four moves, repeated.</h2>
      <p class="mono-label">The method does not change with the medium.</p>
    </aside>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step" data-reveal>
        <span class="step__num">01</span>
        <h3>Draw the line.</h3>
        <p>
          Define the constraint before the feature. What must be true, what will not be
          built, and what would make the work fail. A clear boundary is the first
          design decision.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="step" data-reveal>
        <span class="step__num">02</span>
        <h3>Build the instrument.</h3>
        <p>
          Prototype the hardest part first — the parser edge, the memory model, the
          interaction that carries the product. If the core cannot be made honest, the
          surface will not save it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="step" data-reveal>
        <span class="step__num">03</span>
        <h3>Measure.</h3>
        <p>
          Benchmarks, tests, and limits. Numbers are recorded with their method so they
          can be checked later. A failed result is still a result; it gets published
          rather than redefined.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="step" data-reveal>
        <span class="step__num">04</span>
        <h3>Publish or withhold.</h3>
        <p>
          Finished work is released with its limits included. Unfinished work stays
          private. The archive opens when the work meets the mark, not when the calendar
          asks for a launch.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

